  "query_preview": "../Friday through Sunday/...\n\nA ridge of high pressure \nlasts over the Gulf and panhandle into Friday, however a pattern \nchange begins later Friday into the weekend with a return of a \nseries of systems moving into the area. The first front will move \nin Friday from a low in the Bering Sea, with the front primarily \nlooking to push into the northern Gulf coast Friday night into \nSaturday morning, as the strong high pressure looks to keep the \nfront further westward with lower chances of pushing into the rest\nof the panhandle until Saturday. The timing of this still looks \nto remain uncertain, largely dependent on how quickly the high \npressure begins to break down with this strong low pushing \neastward. It seems that more of the model guidance is keeping the \nfront further west, slowing down the onset of precipitation. \nAlongside the uncertainty of timing, depending on when the front \nbegins to push in will also affect the precipitation type \nexpected; if the front moves in overnight into early Saturday \nmorning, many locations across the northern panhandle may see rain\nwith snow mixing in with the cold airmass in place and below \nfreezing surface temperatures from overnight. However, if it moves\nin during the day Saturday and is delayed further on the timing, \nit is likely to begin as rain and stay predominantly rain, with \nthe warmer air pushing into the area.\n\nThis more active pattern will continue through the weekend as a \nseries of lows move into the Gulf from the south around this main \nparent low as it moves eastward towards the AK Peninsula by \nSunday.",
